<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">What Brennan's Doing Now</h1>

<div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
  <p><small>This is a <a href="https://nownownow.com/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/now page</a>, inspired by Derek Sivers. It's a snapshot of what I'm focused on right now—updated regularly to reflect my current work, projects, and life.</small></p>

  <h2>Life</h2>
  <blockquote>
    <p>"Remember, remember, this is now, and now, and now. Live it, feel it, cling to it. I want to become acutely aware of all I've taken for granted." —Sylvia Plath</p>
  </blockquote>
  <p>I'm 30 years old, currently living in <strong>Calgary, Alberta</strong> on Treaty 7 territory, and planning to move back to my hometown of Winnipeg, Manitoba soon.</p>
  <p>I hold myself accountable on a large number of daily tasks and habits with <a href="https://beeminder.com/brennanbrown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Beeminder</a>: seventeen goals and counting, everything from steps and sleep to word counts and chess puzzles.</p>
  <p>I'm trying to start a community and accessible spaces for writers, makers, and learners through my self-hosted server and in-person events.</p>
  <p>I recently deleted my corporate social media accounts (Facebook, Messenger, Instagram, WhatsApp, Threads, X, Reddit, and Discord). If you want to reach me, please <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>

  <h2>Work</h2>
  <p>My biggest commitment right now is my personal site, <a href="https://brennan.day" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brennan.Day</a>. I've been writing full-time for about eight months—over 450,000 words and 200+ posts. I syndicate my work on <a href="https://blog.brennanbrown.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Medium</a> to make a living through the Medium Partner Program, writing longform essays about tech criticism, culture, and identity. You can help support my work <a href="https://brennan.day/support" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>🍓 Berry House</strong> is the banner under which I do my web development projects. I often do consultations and help out pro bono when asked. One of our current projects is <a href="https://calgarygroups.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Calgary Groups</a>, a wayfinder for Calgary organizations.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong><a href="https://folk.zone" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Folk Zone</a>:</strong> a self-hosted attempt to build the IndieWeb/Fediverse commons myself, running on four machines in my own living space—a federated social community, writing tools, a wiki, pastebin, URL shortener, and more.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="https://fanfiction.lol" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fanfiction.lol</a>:</strong> a fork of <a href="https://archiveofourown.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Archive of Our Own</a> that I host and run—silly, fun, and low-stakes, with more options for archive warnings and relationship dynamic types, no invite queue, and a focus on tag canonization.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="https://brennan.click" target="_blank" rel="noopener">brennan.click</a>:</strong> a wiki-linked digital commonplace book / digital garden with auto-generated stubs and pure-CSS hover transclusion and footnotes.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="https://webwriterscollective.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Web Writers' Collective</a>:</strong> I'm an organiser for this loose effort to help writers find each other and build community across the IndieWeb.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I've shelved plans to teach at <a href="https://fireweed.school" target="_blank" rel="noopener">🔥 Fireweed Writing School</a> for now, and recently did a <a href="https://brennan.day/tending-the-garden-i-have-a-current-state-of-affairs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">public audit of everything I'm running</a>—narrowing my scope to focus on fewer things better.</p>

  <h2>Writing</h2>
  <p>Beyond essays, I write <a href="https://750words.com/person/brennan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">750 words</a> daily, publish technical articles on <a href="https://dev.to/brennan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dev.to</a>, keep a public diary on <a href="https://brennanbrown.dreamwidth.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DreamWidth</a>, and occasionally post new poetry on <a href="https://bkpoetry.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BK Poetry</a>. I microblog on <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/brennan.day" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bluesky</a> and the Fediverse (<a href="https://social.lol/@brennan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@brennan@social.lol</a>), and I'm active on the <a href="https://discourse.32bit.cafe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">32-bit cafe</a> and <a href="https://forum.melonland.net/index.php?action=profile;u=3666" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MelonLand</a> forums and the <a href="https://tildeverse.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tildeverse</a>.</p>
  <p>I'm writing a book—a memoir focusing on the craft of writing—alongside an imagist poetry chapbook. The working title for both is <em>Poetics of Grace</em>. I'm also helping my Mom write her autobiography.</p>

  <h2>Education</h2>
  <p>I graduated in <strong>April 2025</strong> with a <strong>Bachelor of Arts in English (Honours)</strong> from Mount Royal University with a 3.8 GPA. My honours thesis, <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/388769322_HOW_THE_ENGLISH_DEGREE_WILL_SAVE_THE_WORLD_Queering_Decolonizing_and_Democratizing_Literary_Studies_for_Generation_Z" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>How the English Degree Will Save the World</em></a>, examined the transformative potential of literary studies and introduced "bloodwriting" as a bridge between Indigenous knowledge and digital practices.</p>
  <p>I'm continuing my technical education through MOOCs and <a href="https://www.calgarylibrary.ca/read-learn-and-explore/digital-library/linkedin-learning-for-library" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn Learning free of charge via my public library card</a>.</p>

  <h2>Hobbies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Open-source coding on <a href="https://github.com/brennanbrown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> (transitioning to <a href="https://source.tube/brennan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source.tube</a> and <a href="https://gitlab.com/brennankbrown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitLab</a>), tracked with <a href="https://wakatime.com/@brennan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WakaTime</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://lichess.org/@/brennanbrown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chess</a>—a couple of bullet games a day plus at least one rapid game and puzzle</li>
    <li>Daily French practice on <a href="https://www.duolingo.com/profile/brennanbrown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Duolingo</a> and <a href="https://www.clozemaster.com/players/brennanbrown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Clozemaster</a></li>
    <li>Reading tracked on <a href="https://app.thestorygraph.com/profiles/brennanbrown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">StoryGraph</a>; movies on <a href="https://letterboxd.com/brennanbrown" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Letterboxd</a></li>
    <li>Daily meditation, 10,000 steps, and 7.5 hours of sleep, tracked with my Fitbit and Apple Watch</li>
    <li>Retro handheld gaming on a Retroid Pocket 2S</li>
  </ul>

